<title>SWITZERLAND: Richemont H1 operating profit up 31.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Richemont H1 operating profit up 31.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZUG, Switzerland 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30, 1996. (million sterling unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit		     466.2	vs     354.1</p>
<p> Net sales revenue		    2,343.6    vs     2,037.7</p>
<p>Profit attributable to</p>
<p> unitholders			    143.3	vs     152.4</p>
<p> Earnings per unit (stg)	    24.96	vs     26.54</p>
<p>NOTE - Company full name is Compagnie Financiere Richemont AG.  </p>
<p>   Net investment income   12.7 expense    vs 21.1 income</p>
<p>   Profit before tax	 453.5	     vs 375.2</p>
<p>   Profit after tax	  290.7	     vs 248.9</p>
<p>   Tax			   162.8	     vs 126.3</p>
<p>-- RESULTS by activity-</p>
<p>Tobacco-</p>
<p>   Net sales			1,640.0	   vs 1,338.2</p>
<p>   Operating profit	     395.3	     vs 256.6</p>
<p>Luxury goods-</p>
<p>   Net sales			703.6	     vs 699.5</p>
<p>   Operating profit	     110.4	     vs 113.3</p>
<p>Other-</p>
<p>   Operating profit	     1.9 loss	  vs 7.2 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - The results for the latest period do not reflect the impact of the merger of NetHold's European operations with those of French pay-television group Canal+, which was agreed in principle in September 1996.</p>
<p>--Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
